artifacts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-realization characterization output. The summary tables in
# reports/*.csv and reports/*.md are committed on purpose -- diffing two of
# them is how a change in estimator behaviour is noticed. The per-realization
# files are not: a full run at R=1000 across the catalogue is well over a
# million rows, which is a working file, not a record worth keeping in
# history. Regenerate with quarctest.characterize.
reports/*_per_realization.csv

# Crash-recovery state and saved tables from a run in progress. The checkpoint
# is rewritten after every system, so tracking it means a long run leaves the
# working tree permanently dirty. Neither is a record: the committed record is
# reports/characterization*.csv and .md.
reports/.*.ckpt.mat
reports/.*.mat

# Exported dysts ensembles. 129 systems x 100 realizations x 16000 samples of
# float64 is ~1.6 GB of regenerable simulation output; the manifest is small
# and is kept because it carries the reference values and the protocol.
reports/dysts/*.bin
